"1. Rev Port Cardiol. 2017 Nov;36(11):789-798. doi: 10.1016/j.repc.2017.10.006.\nEpub  2017 Nov 20.\n\n2017 Guidelines for the management of arterial hypertension in primary health \ncare in Portuguese-speaking countries.\n\n[Article in English, Portuguese]\n\nOliveira GMM(1), Mendes M(2), Malachias MVB(3), Morais J(4), Filho OM(5), Coelho \nAS(6), Capingana DP(7), Azevedo V(8), Soares I(8), Menete A(9), Ferreira B(9), \nSoares MBDPC(10), Fernandes M(11).\n\nAuthor information:\n(1)Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro (UFRJ), Rio de Janeiro, RJ, Brasil.\n(2)Centro Hospitalar de Lisboa Ocidental, Hospital de Santa Cruz, Carnaxide, \nPortugal. Electronic address: miguel.mendes.md@gmail.com.\n(3)Funda\u00e7\u00e3o Educacional Lucas Machado (Feluma), Faculdade de Ci\u00eancias M\u00e9dicas de \nMinas Gerais, Belo Horizonte, MG, Brasil.\n(4)Centro Hospitalar de Leiria, Hospital de Santo Andr\u00e9, Leiria, Portugal.\n(5)Pontif\u00edcia Universidade Cat\u00f3lica do Paran\u00e1, Curitiba, PR, Brasil.\n(6)Cl\u00ednica Santos Dumont, Lisboa, Portugal.\n(7)Universidade Cuito Cuanavale, Instituto Superior de Ci\u00eancias de Sa\u00fade do \nCuando Cubango, Menongue, Angola.\n(8)Col\u00e9gio da Especialidade de Cardiologia da Ordem dos M\u00e9dicos de Cabo Verde, \nPraia, Cabo Verde.\n(9)Instituto do Cora\u00e7\u00e3o de Mo\u00e7ambique, Maputo, Mo\u00e7ambique; Col\u00e9gio da \nEspecialidade de Cardiologia da Ordem dos M\u00e9dicos de Mo\u00e7ambique, Maputo, \nMo\u00e7ambique.\n(10)Hospital Dr. Ayres de Menezes, S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9, S\u00e3o Tom\u00e9 e Pr\u00edncipe.\n(11)Hospital Am\u00e9rico Boavida, Luanda, Angola.\n\nThe World Health Organization goal's to reduce mortality due to chronic \nnon-communicable diseases by 2% per year demands a huge effort from member \ncountries. This challenge for health professionals requires global political \naction on implementation of social measures, with cost-effective population \ninterventions to reduce chronic non-communicable diseases and their risk \nfactors. Systemic arterial hypertension is highly prevalent in \nPortuguese-speaking countries, and is a major risk factor for complications such \nas stroke, acute myocardial infarction and chronic kidney disease, rivaling \ndyslipidemia and obesity in importance for the development of atherosclerotic \ndisease. Joint actions to implement primary prevention measures can reduce \noutcomes related to hypertensive disease, especially ischemic heart disease and \nstroke. It is essential to ensure the implementation of guidelines for the \nmanagement of systemic hypertension via a continuous process involving \neducational actions, lifestyle changes and guaranteed access to pharmacological \ntreatment.\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2017 Sociedade Portuguesa de Cardiologia. Publicado por Elsevier \nEspa\u00f1a, S.L.U. All rights reserved.\n\nDOI: 10.1016/j.repc.2017.10.006\nPMID: 29162357 [Indexed for MEDLINE]"